{"id": 29, "ts": 1784317007.1577773, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I concur with Agent\u202f2\u2019s shift to Candidate\u202fB as the provisional choice. The discussion has highlighted a critical gap: we have no observations at all on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s ability to stay calm and effective under pressure, yet stress resilience is a non\u2011negotiable safety criterion for long\u2011distance flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB is explicitly noted as \u201chandles stress very well,\u201d directly satisfying that requirement. B also brings strong conscientiousness, solid weather\u2011assessment skills, and excellent computer competence, all of which support technical and decision\u2011quality needs. While B\u2019s \u201cpretentious\u201d demeanor and occasional wrong tone raise legitimate concerns about crew cooperation, these attitude issues are less decisive than the complete absence of stress\u2011resilience evidence for C. Therefore, given the current evidence, Candidate\u202fB remains the stronger overall fit, though we should still seek concrete examples of B\u2019s teamwork and communication style before finalizing.", "thoughts": "We need to produce public message and metadata. Current state: Agent 2 shifted vote to Candidate B. Agent 1 earlier voted Candidate C. Agent 3 earlier was leaning Candidate C but concerned about stress. Now we need to make a contribution. We should decide our current vote. Based on missing stress data for C, B has proven stress resilience. B also has conscientiousness, good weather assessment, technical competence. However B has concerns: pretentious, wrong tone, possibly affecting crew cooperation. Need to weigh. We have no data on B's crew cooperation beyond attitude. But we have no data on C's stress. So maybe we could still favor B, but we could also ask for more info on B's crew cooperation or D's communication. But we need to make a contribution now, referencing discussion, using explicit facts.\n\nWe could say we agree with Agent 2 shifting to B, because stress resilience is non-negotiable and we have no evidence for C. However we still have concerns about B's attitude. We could propose to probe B's crew cooperation further before final. But we need to give a vote now. According to instructions, we must state current recommendation. We can vote B.\n\nThus public message: agree with Agent 2, explain reasoning, mention stress resilience evidence for B, lack for C, mention B's attitude concerns but still outweigh. Also note need to check crew cooperation for B.\n\nProceed."}
